// The Tether-Widows (bible 8.1, saltmarrow-arc.md): the widow herself, at the tether-post once the fourth lamp is lit.
// Until now she was only spoken for (Sable carried word: Quay_Sable_Widow). Answer her here or through Sable; the
// commission's flag is the same either way, and Sable gives her count after (Quay_Sable_Count). She is gone from the
// post once she went in (saltmarrow.widow.decided 2): FlagPresence on her, from the Tetherline's recipe.

title: Tether_Knot
---
<<if flag("saltmarrow.widow.decided") == 1>>
    Knot: Still here. The rope's on the post. I look at it. That's allowed. #still #line:02ba19a
    Knot: You said it, or Sable did. I don't remember which of you. It worked. #still #line:0f3a7e9
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Knot: You're the one who came out. #line:0f86432
Knot: Then it's done. Don't tell me it isn't. I've the rope on already. #line:0ed7bf7
Knot: He went in on Skua's rope to mark the Chain for the Guild. Forty paces. The rope came back. #line:00f908d
Knot: I've measured forty paces on the sand every morning since. I can do forty. #line:092b572
-> He went forty paces. The rope came back. #line:0f44034
    <<voice surveyor saltmarrow>>
    Knot: I know the arithmetic. I wanted it from someone who'd been in. #line:00e24ad
    Knot: Take the rope off me. My hands won't. #line:09a64b8
    <<flag saltmarrow.widow.decided 1>>
-> Then I hold the other end. #line:046a8ae
    <<voice warden saltmarrow>>
    Knot: You'd do that. You don't know me. #line:05d3a83
    Knot: Tonight, on the tide. Don't pull early. Don't pull late, either. #line:03d7cf3
    <<flag saltmarrow.widow.decided 2>>
-> ... #line:00de819
    <<voice drift saltmarrow>>
    Knot: That's an answer. He'd have said that. He never talked me out of anything. #line:09b0ba0
    <<flag saltmarrow.widow.decided 2>>
<<flag saltmarrow.widow.met 1>>
===
